"""Render human-readable research from retained, attributed records; no approval inference."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
read=lambda p:json.loads(p.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
B=read(P/'benchmarks.json');C=read(P/'catalogue.json');bank=read(P/'candidate-bank.json')
def time(s):
 h,rem=divmod(int(s),3600);m,sec=divmod(rem,60)
 return f'{h}:{m:02}:{sec:02}' if h else f'{m}:{sec:02}'
lines=['# Podcast Shorts: improve editorial yield before render volume','',
 'Study date: 8 November 2026. Audience: thought.palace’s reflective, human-story direction.','',
 'The owner is happy with the current captions. The practical failure was selection: only the opening approximately 13 seconds of Peterson clip 04 was compelling; clips 01–03 did not meet this batch’s engagement standard. Full clip 04 is not recorded as approved.','',
 '## What the research actually covers','',
 'The planning study screened 80 Shorts listings, checked live metadata for 14 individual videos and read their available transcripts. These are convenience samples, not a representative causal study. No private completion, retention, rewatch or binge-session metrics were available. No direct full audiovisual playback of all 14 benchmarks is claimed.','',
 f'This implementation catalogued {len(C["episodes"])} public original episodes across six shows. Four members-only Iced Coffee Hour attempts are retained as blocked, with public alternatives added. Fourteen deliberately selected published-caption transcripts are saved and searchable. Episode metadata and available chapter lists were inspected; the full 50 episodes were not watched or transcribed.','',
 'Individual metadata observations below were captured live in the preceding planning turn on the study date. They are dated snapshots, not permanently current counters. `benchmarks.json` retains exact counts, runtime, publication date, method and limitations. Earlier indexed potato-video leads were unavailable in live checks and excluded.','',
 '## Actual Shorts and weaker comparisons','',
 '| Short / channel | Views observed | Duration | Format hypothesis |',
 '| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |']
for b in B['records']:lines.append(f'| [{b["title"]}]({b["url"]}) — {b["channel"]} | {b["observed_views"]:,} | {b["duration_seconds"]}s | {b["format_hypothesis"]} |')
lines += ['',
 'The enjoyment and breakthrough Shorts appeared two days apart on Chris Williamson’s channel. The former challenges a familiar belief; the latter primarily reinforces familiar encouragement. This supports testing specificity and discovery against general encouragement. It does not establish why either performed as it did. Duration, distribution, audience and other differences remain confounders.','',
 'The family-letter comparison matters too: an emotional subject is not sufficient. The high-view partner story puts a concrete crisis in front of the viewer immediately and keeps adding information before its reassuring turn. The contrast is an editorial observation from transcripts, not proof of a measured retention mechanism.','',
 'Successful examples also contradict rigid rules: a 109-second philosophical reframe and a 19-second maxim both found substantial audiences. We should not turn brevity, a particular guest, comedy or rejection of abstract thought into a universal formula.','',
 '## What we should reproduce','',
 '1. **Specific stakes, escalating story, human reversal.** A situation someone can picture is stronger discovery material than a chapter merely labelled success or confidence.','2. **A surprising detail answered through conversation.** Preserve genuine questions and reactions when each adds a new beat. Fast comprehension matters more than deleting every breath.','3. **A familiar problem with an unexpected explanation.** Earn an abstract insight with an example; reject long setup that never changes the viewer’s understanding.','4. **A vulnerable question and a revealing answer.** Keep enough context to understand why the answer matters.','5. **One complete compact thought.** End when it lands; an additional explanation may weaken a good moment.','',
 'These are format hypotheses. YouTube says it favours no particular Shorts format and considers viewer choice, average duration, percentage viewed and satisfaction. There is no minimum posting cadence in that guidance. [YouTube Shorts discovery](https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/11914225?co=YOUTUBE._YTVideoType%3Dshorts&hl=en).','',
 'YouTube’s conversation with Jenny Hoyos supports immediate interest and small complete stories, while remaining creator advice rather than a numeric success law. [Official discussion](https://blog.youtube/creator-and-artist-stories/youtube-shorts-deep-dive/).','',
 'DOAC editor Anthony Smith describes selecting impactful moments and weaving a story before production treatment. His work is on trailers: we adopt emotional construction without withholding a Short’s promised answer. [First-person editor interview](https://becauseofmarketing.com/anthony-smith-the-diary-of-a-ceo/).','',
 '## A scalable discovery funnel','',
 'Catalogue bounded batches from official channels; preserve platform/video identity and access failures. Search successful Shorts back to originals and search original transcripts for situations, distinctive phrases and overlooked anecdotes. Use chapters and heatmaps as leads, not ranking authority. Expand across shows and evergreen episodes when a source has no strong moment.','',
 'Retrieve captions only for deliberately selected episodes, cache them with source identity, and search the local SQLite index. Missing captions and failed retrieval have different statuses. No new models, paid providers or persistent services are required. Download only context windows for actual source study.','',
 'Current shows: Modern Wisdom, The Diary of a CEO, PowerfulJRE, The Iced Coffee Hour, High Performance and This Past Weekend. Every catalogue entry matches the channel ID of its official-channel listing. `show-identities.json` retains corroborating primary-channel/show pages. Identity is not reuse permission.','',
 '## Proof before polish','',
 'For every candidate record: exact opening, context, developing beats, payoff, source ranges, cut proposal, benchmark, rejection risks, review method and reuse basis. The five gates are opening, progression, delivery, payoff and channel fit. A failed gate cannot be offset by a high score elsewhere.','',
 'Prepare an inexpensive full-length proof only after source/rights checks allow production. Review it with sound before 4K caption finishing. Remove redundant setup and repeated agreement, preserve meaningful pauses and genuine reactions, and use accurate source-line restructuring when helpful. Never construct a new speaker claim. Caption style, all-word Difference, italics, music-free output, no foreign branding and resource safeguards remain unchanged.','',
 'The initial bank contains eight screened leads. The owner rejected the offer-story proof for channel fit; it is archived UNSELECTED, not recommended for upload. Seven other leads remain unapproved. The posted-channel correction changes their research order; see review-v2/CHANNEL_FIT.md for primary examples, exact inspection limits and current ranking. Local word/frame evidence is not full listening. Provider review subsequently failed with HTTP 503 and then a bounded timeout; no automatic retries or paid fallback were used. None is production_ready.','',
 '`CANDIDATES.md` provides the prioritised handoff; `candidate-bank.json` retains context and structured checks. `QA_COVERAGE.md` and `validation.json` record exact coverage and tests. No benchmark view count supplies missing retention data.','',
 '## Encourage another worthwhile watch','',
 'Group complementary uploads around decisions, relationships, self-respect and ambition’s costs. Each delivers its own payoff. Suggest a related existing upload on our channel in posting notes; do not add a forced part-two cliffhanger or invented channel symbol. [YouTube Related Video](https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/14075157?hl=en) requires advanced feature access and a public/unlisted target on the same channel.','',
 'Use similar topics and familiar formats to build recognition. Returning-viewer growth is a longer-term loyalty signal, not measured individual binge sessions. [YouTube audience guidance](https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/10246996?hl=en). Meta also describes personalised Reel ranking with early-dismissal and time-spent signals, not a universal editing recipe. [Meta system card](https://transparency.meta.com/features/explaining-ranking/ig-reels-chaining).','',
 '## Learn from actual outcomes','',
 '`results.py` retains legacy --avd as average percentage viewed. Seconds now have their own --avg-view-duration-seconds field. Unknown metrics remain null/N/A, publication-age snapshots stay separate, and there is no blanket 85/85 success cutoff. Owner selection is stored independently, including excerpt_only so an approved opening does not silently become an approved complete edit.','',
 'Record real production time, including effort spent on rejected clips. Compute minutes per accepted clip only when those time records are complete; do not invent historic times. Compare public views, engaged views, stayed-to-watch, average duration, percentage viewed, shares and subscriber conversion at comparable ages when available. The first success measure is how many proposed edits the owner actually chooses to publish.','',
 '## Deliberately rejected or held leads','',
 '- Jimmy Carr’s general confidence explanation at DOAC approximately 1:42:45: sound advice, but largely explanatory and familiar; held rather than padding the bank.','- James Smith’s worth/performance passage around 1:07:52: starts with a quoted lesson and moves into abstract explanation, then promotion; not a stronger cold opening for this batch.','- Neumann’s already-successful lost-everything partner story: retained as a verified structural benchmark, not presented as an overlooked fresh discovery. Original context also contains a correction to the host’s wording that must not be distorted.','- Caleb’s religious-healing anecdote: not selected; uncertain factual implications and the channel’s current human-story brief make other passages preferable.','- Generic health, political and market episodes remain metadata-only catalogue entries; their presence does not approve them for this channel.','',
 'A 30.36-second offer-story content proof was archived in Exports at the owner’s request, explicitly UNSELECTED after rejection. No new upload-ready clip is approved. Owner permission is confirmed for DOAC episode QMzxNfX-uAg; other new-source permissions remain unknown. Permission never substitutes for channel fit.','']
(P/'RESEARCH_REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines),encoding='utf-8')
out=['# Candidate bank — source discovery, not upload-ready edits','',
 'Eight screened leads, including one explicit owner rejection; do not fill the bank to 20. Primary channel-fit review and current study order: review-v2/CHANNEL_FIT.md. Source/channel metadata verified. Published-caption boundaries are approximate and require word/frame alignment. Read pending opening/delivery gates before production. Unknown reuse permission remains separate.','']
for b in sorted(bank,key=lambda b:({'study_channel_fit':0,'secondary_fit':1,'hold_fit':2,'rejected_owner_fit':3}.get(b.get('priority'),3),b['id'])):
 ranges=' + '.join(time(a)+'–'+time(z) for a,z in b['segments']); url=b['source_url']+'&t='+str(int(min(a for a,z in b['segments'])))
 out += [f'## {b["id"]}: {b["title"]}','',f'**Original:** [{b["source_title"]}]({url})',f'**Proposed source ranges:** {ranges}; approximately {b["approximate_duration"]:.1f}s before further tightening.',f'**Status:** {b["status"]}; opening {b["checks"]["opening"]}; delivery {b["checks"]["delivery"]}; reuse basis {b["reuse_basis"]}.','',
  f'**Priority:** {b.get("priority","unassigned")} (study_channel_fit: inspect first, not approved; secondary_fit: conditional; hold_fit: no proof yet; rejected_owner_fit: archive only).','',
  f'**Opening:** “{b["opening"]}”','',f'**Context:** {b["context"]}','',f'**Payoff:** {b["payoff"]}','',f'**Cut proposal:** {b["cut_proposal"]}','',f'**Benchmark match:** {b["benchmark"]}','', '**Rejection risks:** '+' '.join(b['risks']),'']
 if b.get('channel_match_review'):out += ['**Posted-channel match:** '+b['channel_match_review']['reason'],'']
 if b.get('review_findings'):out += ['**Audiovisual second opinion:** '+b['review_findings'],'']
 if b.get('visual_review'):out += ['**Source-frame study:** '+b['visual_review']['finding'],'']
 if b['av_review'].get('attempt'):out += ['**Remaining evidence:** '+b['av_review']['attempt'],'']
 out += ['Full timestamped surrounding context is retained per entry in candidate-bank.json. No scores override a failed or pending editorial gate. Further audiovisual study, if available, is recorded in source-review; transcript fluency has not been presented as listening.','']
(P/'CANDIDATES.md').write_text('\n'.join(out),encoding='utf-8')
print('Wrote RESEARCH_REPORT.md and CANDIDATES.md')
